content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing vibration of 8.3 mm/s is in Zone D (red, 7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The applicable limit is the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary in the HF-300 manual, Figure 3. The reading exceeds it by 1.2 mm/s, so the boundary ambiguity does not matter. The manual says to classify the highest bearing-housing reading and act on its zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Site standard SSP-07 says vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone (Zone D) requires stopping the machine immediately and notifying the reliability engineer before restart. This applies to P-114 now.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature of 70 C equals the top of the documented normal band ('Normal up to 70 C'). It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip limits in the HF-300 specification table. The SSP-07 temperature-based P1 trigger (above alarm limit) is not met. Priority P1 is set because of the Zone D vibration and the mandatory stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage reported. The shaft-seal leakage symptom in the troubleshooting table does not apply, so mechanical seal replacement is not indicated by this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the housing temperature is at the top of the normal band.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. It is a listed cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the high reading is localised at the drive-end bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. It is a listed cause of high bearing temperature and should be checked alongside the above.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-114 immediately. Notify the reliability engineer, whose clearance is required before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any internal work, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. Close and lock the suction and discharge valves. Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool against the tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the bearing grease quantity for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings for wear, noise or overheating. If either shows wear, replace both bearings as a pair (DE 6312-C3 and NDE 6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed, prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment, as the assembly mass is 68 kg. Inspect the impeller for imbalance or damage while it is accessible.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check NPSH and suction conditions for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten fasteners to manual Table 5, which applies to this serial. Table 5 torque values are not in the evidence provided; obtain them before reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or the bearing housing, re-align with the laser tool to 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On restart, which requires reliability engineer approval, measure vibration on both bearing housings. Confirm the highest reading is out of Zone D, ideally at or below 4.5 mm/s (Zone A/B). Confirm housing temperature stays at or below 70 C, well under the 80 C alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair with the NDE bearing if wear is found)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with the DE bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, to be replaced whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately because of the Zone D vibration. Notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit: drain and vent first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, which exceeds the 25 kg threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair), if wear is confirmed: 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement (4.0 h, 2 technicians) is not planned, because no leakage was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with HF3-450B and raises gland torque to 30 Nm. It applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, which is below that range. Therefore the original manual applies: use HF3-450 and Table 5 if the seal is ever replaced, not HF3-450B or 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The temperature criteria do not conflict with the vibration criteria. At 70 C the temperature is within the manufacturer's normal band and does not trigger the SSP-07 temperature P1 rule. The vibration criterion (Zone D) independently mandates the stop under both the manual and SSP-07. The stricter vibration-based action governs.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Manual Table 5 fastener torque values are not included in the evidence and are needed for reassembly.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing housing vibration reading was not reported; the manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest classified.",
    "The vibration history and trend for P-114 are not provided, so it is unknown how quickly the reading rose.",
    "Is the raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required under SSP-07.",
    "A detailed bearing replacement procedure, grease type and grease quantity are not given in the evidence.",
    "Does bearing replacement on the HF-300 require the casing joint to be opened (triggering gasket replacement) or disturbing the mechanical seal? The evidence does not state this.",
    "Is the reported 8.3 mm/s an RMS value, as used by Figure 3? The report does not specify.",
    "NPSH available and required data for this installation are not provided, so cavitation cannot be assessed from the evidence."
  ]
}
